  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="03b01828-ce1e-5fc8-a975-38569682088b" activityNameId="08e68f80-1914-563b-836c-5c40c30a35f2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Manganese concentrate, at beneficiation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Manganese concentrate, at beneficiation
The module describes the production of manganese ore in 1994 for a world-wide production average. It is designed for the use of manganese ore as intermediary product in the production of ferromanganese and manganese metal. For the use of this module in the battery manufacture, the data quality may not be sufficient.;
UUID: f2604d57-9474-36dc-9219-c04eedc6f657
The module includes a mining and a beneficiation step with the mining infrastructure and disposal of overburden and tailings (see part II "Auxiliary Processes").
Location: This module relates to the global situation. Some modules used like lime, blasting and transport originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe
Technology: Mining is done 70% open pit and 30% underground, followed by a beneficiation of the ore trough classification. Overburden and tailings are non-sulphidic , they are disposed near the mining site.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 23.5 million tonnes in 1995
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f2604d57-9474-36dc-9219-c04eedc6f657.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
